<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">It's Now or Never (Elvis Presley; words by Aaron Schroeder and Wally Gold)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new English words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">There's No Tomorrow (Tony Martin; words by Al Hoffman, Leo Corday and Leon Carr)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1949</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, new English words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Down from His Glory (William E. Booth-Clibborn)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1921</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, hymn words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">First English version (Charles W. Harrison)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1915</span><span class="sg-chain-h">translation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">&quot;Just One Cornetto&quot; television jingle</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1980s</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody, advertising words</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">101 Gang Songs (Bing Crosby)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1961</span><span class="sg-chain-h">in a medley</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Just One (ReMAXed Remix) (Susan Boyle)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2026</span><span class="sg-chain-h">adapted as a dance version</span></li></ul></section>
